{id:6007,q:"A job applicant earns a difficult certification to show ability. Why can the certification work as a signal?",options:["It is costly enough that weaker applicants may be less likely to imitate it","It hides the applicant's type from employers","It monitors the applicant after hiring","It changes the firm's transfer price"],a:0,tag:"signaling",type:"diagnostic",objective:"LO19.4",feedback:"A signal is more credible when it is harder or more costly for lower-quality types to copy."}
